    <section class="ds-section" id="selected-look">
        <h2 class="ds-section__title">Selected look</h2>
        <p class="ds-section__blurb">
            The rule says selected has one look: <code>--color-control-selected-bg</code> with
            <code>--color-link</code> text. This row puts every component's selected or current state next to
            that reference, grouped by the mechanism it actually uses. Four show up today: the tinted fill,
            a solid primary fill, a raised ink pill, and an underline — plus a fifth inside menus, where the
            radio or checkbox carries the state and the row stays untinted. Decide which of these are
            deliberate and which are drift.
        </p>
        <h3 class="ds-group__title">Tint and blue text</h3>
