    </section>
    <section class="ds-section" id="menus">
        <h2 class="ds-section__title">Menus and panels</h2>
        <p class="ds-section__blurb">
            The four panel-shaped components side by side. Pin them open to compare the rows directly: the
            row height (<code>--menu-row-height</code>, which is the medium control height on a fine
            pointer), the inset pill and its hover, where the state indicator sits and what it is (link-blue
            text in the menu, a radio in options, a checkbox in select, nothing in the bare popover), the
            section headings, and the search field's height and focus ring against the input in the
            alignment row above. Pinning turns off outside-click dismissal; Escape still closes the
            frontmost one.
        </p>
        <div class="ds-check-controls">
            <ol-toggle id="menus-pin" label="Pin open" data-ds-pin-menus>
            </ol-toggle>
        </div>
        <div class="ds-example__output ds-menu-row">
            <ol-tooltip content="A tooltip — the one surface without a border or shadow">
                <ol-button variant="ghost">
                    Tooltip
                </ol-button>
            </ol-tooltip>
            <ol-popover aria-label="Playground popover" data-ds-pinnable>
                <ol-button slot="trigger">
                    Popover
                </ol-button>
                {{ pop.menu("200px") }}
            </ol-popover>
            <ol-menu-popover label="Sort by" value="new" aria-label="Playground menu" items='{{ MENU_ITEMS }}' data-ds-pinnable>
            </ol-menu-popover>
            <ol-select-popover label="Language" placeholder="Filter languages…" unselected-heading="LANGUAGES" selected='["en"]' aria-label="Playground select" items='{{ MANY_LANGUAGES }}' data-ds-pinnable>
                <ol-button slot="trigger">
                    Language
                </ol-button>
            </ol-select-popover>
            <ol-options-popover label="Genre" selected="fiction" aria-label="Playground options" items='{{ OPTIONS_ITEMS }}' data-ds-pinnable>
            </ol-options-popover>
        </div>
        <div class="ds-menu-row__stage" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <h3 class="ds-group__title">Row anatomy</h3>
        <p class="ds-group__blurb">
            The light-DOM row the design docs use as the reference, next to the pieces a Lit row adds. A
            heading, a plain row, a hovered-looking row, the current row in the menu's style, and a divider.
            Compare against the pinned panels above.
        </p>
        <div class="ds-example__output">
            <nav class="ds-demo-menu ds-demo-menu--panel" aria-label="Row anatomy">
                <div class="ds-demo-menu__heading">Sort order</div>
                <a class="ds-demo-menu__link" href="#menus">Relevance</a>
                <a class="ds-demo-menu__link is-current" href="#menus">Most Recent</a>
                <a class="ds-demo-menu__link" href="#menus">Top Rated</a>
                <hr class="ds-demo-menu__divider">
                <a class="ds-demo-menu__link" href="#menus">
                    <ol-icon name="pencil" size="sm">
                    </ol-icon>
                    With an icon
                </a>
            </nav>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="ds-section" id="surfaces">
        <h2 class="ds-section__title">Surfaces and text</h2>
        <p class="ds-section__blurb">
            Every surface a control or a line of text can land on, with the text tokens painted on it and
            their measured contrast, the border weights as rules, and a small set of raised controls. Read it
            for three things: which text tokens are safe on which surface (muted ink is AA on white and
            the lightest raised surface only), whether a raised control still reads as raised when its
            surface is already off-white, and whether the status washes and the selected tint sit in the
            same family or fight.
        </p>
        <div class="ds-surface-grid">
            {% for token, title, note in SURFACES %}
                <section class="ds-surface" style="background: var({{ token }});">
                    <header class="ds-surface__header">
                        <h3 class="ds-surface__title">{{ title }}</h3>
                        <code class="ds-surface__token"
                              data-ds-copy
                              data-ds-copy-text="var({{ token }})"
                              title="Copy var({{ token }})">{{ token }}</code>
                    </header>
                    <ul class="ds-surface__text">
                        {% for text_token, text_title in TEXT_TOKENS %}
                            <li class="ds-surface__text-row">
                                <span class="ds-surface__sample" style="color: var({{ text_token }});">{{ text_title }} — the quick brown fox</span>
                                <span class="ds-surface__contrast"
                                      data-ds-contrast-for="{{ text_token }}"
                                      data-ds-contrast-on="{{ token }}"></span>
                            </li>
                        {% endfor %}
                    </ul>
                    <div class="ds-surface__rules">
                        <span class="ds-surface__rule ds-surface__rule--extra-subtle"
                              title="--color-border-extra-subtle"></span>
                        <span class="ds-surface__rule ds-surface__rule--subtle"
                              title="--color-border-subtle"></span>
                        <span class="ds-surface__rule ds-surface__rule--muted"
                              title="--color-border-muted"></span>
                        <span class="ds-surface__rule ds-surface__rule--default"
                              title="--color-border"></span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ds-surface__controls">
                        <ol-button size="small">
                            Button
                        </ol-button>
                        <ol-button size="small" variant="ghost">
                            Ghost
                        </ol-button>
                        <ol-button size="small" selected>
                            Selected
                        </ol-button>
                        <ol-chip size="small">
                            Chip
                        </ol-chip>
                    </div>
                    <p class="ds-surface__note">{{ note }}</p>
                </section>
            {% endfor %}
            <section class="ds-surface ds-surface--inverse">
                <header class="ds-surface__header">
                    <h3 class="ds-surface__title">Inverse</h3>
                    <code class="ds-surface__token"
                          data-ds-copy
                          data-ds-copy-text="var(--color-surface-inverse)"
                          title="Copy var(--color-surface-inverse)">--color-surface-inverse</code>
                </header>
                <ul class="ds-surface__text">
                    <li class="ds-surface__text-row">
                        <span class="ds-surface__sample ds-surface__sample--inverse">Inverse — the quick brown fox</span>
                        <span class="ds-surface__contrast"
                              data-ds-contrast-for="--color-text-inverse"
                              data-ds-contrast-on="--color-surface-inverse"></span>
                    </li>
                </ul>
                <p class="ds-surface__note">Tooltips and dark chips. No control is specified for this surface; a secondary button dropped here would paint its own white fill.</p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="ds-section" id="focus">
        <h2 class="ds-section__title">Focus rings</h2>
        <p class="ds-section__blurb">
            Click into the first field, then Tab along the row. Every ring should be the same 2px of
            <code>--color-focus-ring</code> at the same distance from the control's edge. Two mechanisms are
            in use today — an <code>outline</code> that sits outside the rounded box, and a
            <code>box-shadow</code> that hugs it — and the offsets range from 2px outside to 2px inside, so
            a ring that looks tighter or looser than its neighbour is the thing to note. Inside the pinned
            menus above, rows show focus as a fill rather than a ring.
        </p>
        <div class="ds-example__output">
            <div class="ds-strip ds-strip--focus">
                {% call specimen("Input", "box-shadow? outline?") %}
                    <input class="control-row__field ds-focus-start"
                           type="text"
                           value="Start here"
                           aria-label="Focus start">
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Button", "outline, 2px out") %}
                    <ol-button>
                        Button
                    </ol-button>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Primary", "outline, 2px out") %}
                    <ol-button variant="primary">
                        Primary
                    </ol-button>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Icon button", "outline, 2px out") %}
                    <ol-button shape="icon" aria-label="Search">
                        <ol-icon name="search" size="sm">
                        </ol-icon>
                    </ol-button>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Switch", "box-shadow, flush") %}
                    <ol-toggle label="Switch">
                    </ol-toggle>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Toggle button", "box-shadow, flush") %}
                    <ol-toggle variant="button" label="Readable" sublabel="4.6M">
                    </ol-toggle>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Chip", "box-shadow, flush") %}
                    <ol-chip>
                        Fiction
                    </ol-chip>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Segmented", "outline, 2px in") %}
                    <ol-segmented-control accessible-label="Focus segmented">
                        <ol-segment value="a">
                            One
                        </ol-segment>
                        <ol-segment value="b">
                            Two
                        </ol-segment>
                    </ol-segmented-control>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Pagination", "outline, 2px out") %}
                    <ol-pagination total-pages="2" current-page="1" label-pagination="Focus pagination">
                    </ol-pagination>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Tabs", "outline, 2px in") %}
                    <ol-tabs accessible-label="Focus tabs">
                        <a slot="tab" href="#focus-tab-a">One</a>
                        <a slot="tab" href="#focus-tab-b">Two</a>
                        <div id="focus-tab-a"></div>
                        <div id="focus-tab-b"></div>
                    </ol-tabs>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Shelf button", "outline, 2px in") %}
                    <ol-shelf-button user-key="{{ user_key }}" work-key="/works/OL27448W" book-title="Pride and Prejudice">
                    </ol-shelf-button>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Menu row", "outline, 2px in") %}
                    <nav class="ds-demo-menu ds-demo-menu--inline" aria-label="Focus menu row">
                        <a class="ds-demo-menu__link" href="#focus">Edit</a>
                    </nav>
                {% endcall %}
                {% call specimen("Link", "browser default") %}
                    <a href="#focus">Plain link</a>
                {% endcall %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="ds-section" id="density">
        <h2 class="ds-section__title">Density</h2>
        <p class="ds-section__blurb">
            A realistic toolbar at each control size. Checks that the sizes stay usable together, not just
            individually — the small row is what most filter bars actually use.
        </p>
        {% for size in ["small", "medium", "large"] %}
            <h3 class="ds-group__title">{{ size | capitalize }}</h3>
            <div class="ds-example__output ds-pattern-bar">
                <ol-button {% if size != "medium" %}size="{{ size }}"{% endif %} variant="secondary">
                    Filter
                </ol-button>
                <ol-segmented-control {% if size != "medium" %}size="{{ size }}"{% endif %} accessible-label="View, {{ size }}">
                    <ol-segment value="grid">
                        Grid
                    </ol-segment>
                    <ol-segment value="list">
                        List
                    </ol-segment>
                </ol-segmented-control>
                <ol-select-popover label="Language" search-threshold="999" aria-label="Density select, {{ size }}" items='{{ SELECT_ITEMS }}'>
                    <ol-button slot="trigger" {% if size != "medium" %}size="{{ size }}"{% endif %} variant="secondary">
                        Language
                    </ol-button>
                </ol-select-popover>
                <ol-menu-popover label="Sort by" value="relevance" aria-label="Density sort, {{ size }}" items='{{ MENU_ITEMS }}'>
                    <ol-button slot="trigger" {% if size != "medium" %}size="{{ size }}"{% endif %}>
                        Sort by
                    </ol-button>
                </ol-menu-popover>
                <span class="ds-pattern-bar__spacer"></span>
                <ol-button {% if size != "medium" %}size="{{ size }}"{% endif %} variant="primary">
                    Apply
                </ol-button>
            </div>
        {% endfor %}
    </section>
    <section class="ds-section" id="long-content">
        <h2 class="ds-section__title">Long content</h2>
